"Hojita Discordia" <nethack.addict.hojita@neverbox.com> wrote

> I'd say balancing the artifacts would make them more interesting.  If
> I had to arbitrarily change (non-quest) artifacts to make some more
> appealing (and others less appealing), here are some ideas:
>
> Grayswandir: 1.5x damage instead of double

Fair enough, except that this makes Firebrand and Frostbrand significantly
better.  As it stands, GS and the FBs are just about equivalent, with each
better in a few situations.  So if you do this, turn down all 3 of these
to 1.5x or 1.75x.

Alternatively, change the "double damage" portion of the weapon to apply
to fewer of the bonuses -- say, double base damage but not double
enchantment.

> Trollsbane: kills trolls instantly (or trolls hit/killed by it don't
> regen?)

Trolls killed by it don't regen.

(Someone made the suggestion you should have the choice... I think you
already do.  If the troll is about to die, finish it off with a different
weapon if you want it to regen.)

> Dragonsbane: kills dragons instantly (or dragons always leave scales?)

Both of these would be extremely overpowering in the mid-game, and useless
once you had *DSM.

> Werebane: werefoo cannot summon help when wielded
> Ogresmasher: kills ogres instantly
> Orcrist: 3X damage to orcs instead

Problem with the last 5 is they still remain very specialized.  Adding
even a small, but general, bonus to these would be more likely to make
them used (say, +d4 to everything, and retain extra properties against
ogres / werefoo / dragons / trolls)

> Demonbane: does 2X damage against riders, as well (or more??)
> Tsurugi: always insta-kill engulfers

I like both of these.

Perhaps demonbane could also increase the chance of A being created
peaceful (and same for Sunsword).  If you're wielding an angelic /
antidemon weapon, they're more likely to treat you as a friend.

> Grimtooth (I forget this even exists sometimes): always poisoned

Nice.  Would be fairly useful early game.

What about Snickersnee?  Do you think it needs any sort of extra bonus?

> To balance the large amount of "insta-kill" weapons (not that a
> combat-wombat can't insta-kill most anything anyways by the end game),
> I also propose a limit on artifacts found in the game to be a
> predetermined random number from 3-6 (barring named, quest, and
> invocation artifacts).

As mentioned before, this would make Astral easier -- if you have enough
artifacts, there's no chance anything on Astral will be wielding Vorpy.

One way to re-balance this might be to give player monsters on Astral a
chance of wielding quest artifact weapons, rather than just general
artifact weapons.

> Also, what about the idea of slightly random to-hit and damage
> bonuses? That way you wouldn't know exactly how good each weapon is.

No.  This doesn't make you any more likely to choose another weapon -- 
you'll still most likely pick the one with the highest nominal / average
bonus.  It just means you might get screwed on occasion...



